# KV5-5, the Mac, 2026-11-06: sharing by reference. CopyKV maps the source's blocks into the destination's table and counts them; a slot about to write into a block another slot names first takes its own (copy on write). Shared lock for builds and tests; G3b under the exclusive lock, on AC.

== what changed
kvcopy.go: CopyKV moves no rows. Each of dst's entries in [start, end) names src's block, kvRefs counts it, and the block dst held is released to kvFree. kvOwn(s, lo, hi) gives slot s its own block for every block overlapping a write that another entry also names: a block from kvFree, holding a copy of the rows below lo (rows at or past lo are the write's, as CUDA's kvMap). kvBlocksInUse is the pool's own count.
Every write site owns first: decode (setPos, so the executor's commit and the synchronous paths alike), ForwardBatch, the prefill pass, the E-model and paged-MoE layer-major prefills, the batched step's rows, UploadKV, and the greedy chain, which owns the rest of its slot's table before it opens since it commits ahead of the host.
A copy on write is a host memcpy of mapped pages, with nothing of the resident in flight at any of those sites. kvFree cannot run dry: the pools hold every slot's table, so a block named twice leaves one free.
The pools' bytes are unchanged. Sharing frees blocks, not bytes; the pool banner, serve check's row and borrowing past a slot's share are KV5-6.

== red first
TestKVPages_shareByReference against main's CopyKV (rows copied; kept, with this slice's helpers, so the test builds): "sharing freed 0 blocks; want 20, the preamble held once", on all four arms.

== TestKVPages_shareByReference (MC3 fixture, 3 slots; f16 and int8 KV, in-order and scrambled tables)
Slot 0 prefills a 640-row preamble; slots 1 and 2 take it by CopyKV: 20 blocks freed, the preamble held once. Each slot prefills its own suffix and decodes. Then the slots rewind into blocks the others still share, by every writer: a prefill from 600, the step at 500, ForwardBatch at 400, a decode at 402 (slot 0); the verify at 340, UploadKV at 280, a decode at 281 (slot 1); a decode at 200 and the greedy chain from 150 (slot 2). After each write, every slot's K/V over its valid history so far is read back through its table.
Held: every logit and every K/V buffer equal to the reference, a fresh resident where each slot prefilled the preamble itself. PASS on all four arms.
The K/V check is the one that catches a leak: on this fixture's peaked attention a leaked row moves no logit. A first version compared only at the end, after the slots had rewound below the leaked rows, and missed two plants; it now records after every write.

== TestKVPages_shareByReferenceLayerMajor
gemma4-emodel-tiny (its batched pass declined by a raised floor, so the layer-major pass runs) and mixtral-tiny paged at 3 slots, each copied with a 2,048-position window, 2 slots: a 128-row preamble shared, slot 1's suffix, slot 0 rewinding into the shared block; slot 1's K/V equals its own-preamble reference, and the layer-major pass's own counter shows it ran. PASS.

== plants, 8 of 8 red (04:15 to 04:21)
kvOwn removed at: decode (setPos), ForwardBatch, the prefill pass, the batched step, UploadKV, the greedy chain (each caught by TestKVPages_shareByReference), the E-model layer-major prefill and the paged-MoE layer-major prefill (each caught by TestKVPages_shareByReferenceLayerMajor).

== G3b on the real 1.5B, 2026-11-06 04:46 to 04:48 PST (lock requested 04:34:47, released 04:48:54): PASS
TestKVPages_G3bRealPreamble, GOINFER_METAL_MC3=1: qwen2.5-coder-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf from ~/models, int4, 4 slots, MacBookPro18,3, on AC, exclusive lock. Four conversations share a 16,384-token preamble, prefilled once in 1,024-row passes and taken by three CopyKV calls: 768 blocks freed, 268 in use after, so the preamble is held once. Each conversation's 16 greedy tokens after its own 64-token suffix equal that conversation run alone on a slot of its own, prefilled the same way, token for token, all four. Wall 140 s.
Not read here: the registered form's serve-level reading through decoder's prefix reuse. The resident-level test drives CopyKV as decoder's KV manager does.

